==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|ψυχή||soul|tr=psukhē|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|ἰατρεία||healing|tr=iatreia|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} from {{term|ἰάομαι||I heal|tr=iaomai|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/saɪˈkaɪ.əˌtɹi/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|psychiatries}}

# {{medicine}} The branch of [[medicine]] that subjectively [[diagnose]]s, treats, and studies mental illness and [[behavioural]] conditions.

====Derived terms====
* [[psychiatric]]
* [[psychiatrist]]

